# Perilous Snare: "Max speed — {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature or Vehicle you control. Activate only as a
# sorcery." Max speed means "as long as your speed is 4, this object has [the ability]" (CR 702.178a). Bot1's speed is 1
# from the Snare on turn 1 (CR 704.5aa) and Lightning Bolts raise it on turns 1, 3 and 5 (CR 702.179d). At speed 3 on
# turn 3 the ability is not offered, though the Snare is untapped, it is Bot1's main phase and Bot1's uncrewed Smuggler's
# Copter is there; at speed 4 on turn 5 it is, and puts a counter on the Copter, a Vehicle that is not a creature. Bot2's
# Ornithopter is refused as a target (not "you control"), and so is Bot1's Mox Ruby (neither a creature nor a Vehicle). In turn 7's upkeep it is refused again, the Snare untapped:
# "only as a sorcery" (CR 602.5d). In the main phase it targets Bot1's own Ornithopter, a creature, which Bot2 Bolts in
# response: the ability does nothing (CR 608.2b), and no counter goes anywhere. A counter on a creature of Bot1's is in
# speed-is-gained-with-control-of-a-snare-and-max-speed-is-its-controllers.

